asammūḍhaḥ sa martyeṣu
sarva-pāpaiḥ pramucyate\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2836,\"bb\":2510,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/3/b2510/\",\"shadow_value\":\"yaḥ – anyone who; mām – Me; ajam – unborn; anādim – without beginning; ca – also; vetti – knows; loka – of the planets; mahā-īśvaram – the supreme master; asammūḍhaḥ – undeluded; saḥ – he; martyeṣu – among those subject to death; sarva-pāpaiḥ – from all sinful reactions; pramucyate – is delivered.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"yaḥ\",\"translation\":\"anyone who\"},{\"word\":\"mām\",\"translation\":\"Me\"},{\"word\":\"ajam\",\"translation\":\"unborn\"},{\"word\":\"anādim\",\"translation\":\"without beginning\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"vetti\",\"translation\":\"knows\"},{\"word\":\"loka\",\"translation\":\"of the planets\"},{\"word\":\"mahā-īśvaram\",\"translation\":\"the supreme master\"},{\"word\":\"asammūḍhaḥ\",\"translation\":\"undeluded\"},{\"word\":\"saḥ\",\"translation\":\"he\"},{\"word\":\"martyeṣu\",\"translation\":\"among those subject to death\"},{\"word\":\"sarva-pāpaiḥ\",\"translation\":\"from all sinful reactions\"},{\"word\":\"pramucyate\",\"translation\":\"is delivered\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2837,\"bb\":2511,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/3/b2511/\",\"body_value\":\"He who knows Me as the unborn, as the beginningless, as the Supreme Lord of all the worlds – he only, undeluded among men, is freed from all sins.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2838,\"bb\":2512,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/3/b2512/\",\"body_value\":\"As stated in the Seventh Chapter (7.3), manuṣyāṇāṁ sahasreṣu kaścid yatati siddhaye: those who are trying to elevate themselves to the platform of spiritual realization are not ordinary men; they are superior to millions and millions of ordinary men who have no knowledge of spiritual realization. But out of those actually trying to understand their spiritual situation, one who can come to the understanding that Kṛṣṇa is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the proprietor of everything, the unborn, is the most successful spiritually realized person. In that stage only, when one has fully understood Kṛṣṇa’s supreme position, can one be free completely from all sinful reactions.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2839,\"bb\":2513,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/3/b2513/\",\"body_value\":\"Here the Lord is described by the word aja, meaning “unborn,” but He is distinct from the living entities who are described in the Second Chapter as aja. The Lord is different from the living entities who are taking birth and dying due to material attachment. The conditioned souls are changing their bodies, but His body is not changeable. Even when He comes to this material world, He comes as the same unborn; therefore in the Fourth Chapter it is said that the Lord, by His internal potency, is not under the inferior, material energy, but is always in the superior energy.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2840,\"bb\":2514,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/3/b2514/\",\"body_value\":\"In this verse the words vetti loka-maheśvaram indicate that one should know that Lord Kṛṣṇa is the supreme proprietor of the planetary systems of the universe. He was existing before the creation, and He is different from His creation. All the demigods were created within this material world, but as far as Kṛṣṇa is concerned, it is said that He is not created; therefore Kṛṣṇa is different even from the great demigods like Brahmā and Śiva. And because He is the creator of Brahmā, Śiva and all the other demigods, He is the Supreme Person of all planets.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2841,\"bb\":2515,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/3/b2515/\",\"body_value\":\"Śrī Kṛṣṇa is therefore different from everything that is created, and anyone who knows Him as such immediately becomes liberated from all sinful reactions. One must be liberated from all sinful activities to be in the knowledge of the Supreme Lord. Only by devotional service can He be known and not by any other means, as stated in Bhagavad-gītā.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2842,\"bb\":2516,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/3/b2516/\",\"body_value\":\"One should not try to understand Kṛṣṇa as a human being. As stated previously, only a foolish person thinks Him to be a human being. This is again expressed here in a different way. A man who is not foolish, who is intelligent enough to understand the constitutional position of the Godhead, is always free from all sinful reactions.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2843,\"bb\":2517,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/3/b2517/\",\"body_value\":\"If Kṛṣṇa is known as the son of Devakī, then how can He be unborn? That is also explained in Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam: When He appeared before Devakī and Vasudeva, He was not born as an ordinary child; He appeared in His original form, and then He transformed Himself into an ordinary child.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2844,\"bb\":2518,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/3/b2518/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 10.3\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 10.3\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",