\":\"/en/library/bg/10/6/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 6\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":2846,\"bb\":568245,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"बुद्धिर्ज्ञानमसम्मोह: क्षमा सत्यं दम: शम: ।
सुखं दु:खं भवोऽभावो भयं चाभयमेव च ॥ ४ ॥
अहिंसा समता तुष्टिस्तपो दानं यशोऽयश: ।
भवन्ति भावा भूतानां मत्त एव पृथग्विधा: ॥ ५ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2847,\"bb\":2520,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2520/\",\"body_value\":\"buddhir jñānam asammohaḥ
kṣamā satyaṁ damaḥ śamaḥ
sukhaṁ duḥkhaṁ bhavo ’bhāvo
bhayaṁ cābhayam eva ca\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2848,\"bb\":2521,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2521/\",\"body_value\":\"ahiṁsā samatā tuṣṭis
tapo dānaṁ yaśo ’yaśaḥ
bhavanti bhāvā bhūtānāṁ
matta eva pṛthag-vidhāḥ\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2849,\"bb\":2522,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2522/\",\"shadow_value\":\"buddhiḥ – intelligence; jñānam – knowledge; asammohaḥ – freedom from doubt; kṣamā – forgiveness; satyam – truthfulness; damaḥ – control of the senses; śamaḥ – control of the mind; sukham – happiness; duḥkham – distress; bhavaḥ – birth; abhāvaḥ – death; bhayam – fear; ca – also; abhayam – fearlessness; eva – also; ca – and; ahiṁsā – nonviolence; samatā – equilibrium; tuṣṭiḥ – satisfaction; tapaḥ – penance; dānam – charity; yaśaḥ – fame; ayaśaḥ – infamy; bhavanti – come about; bhāvāḥ – natures; bhūtānām – of living entities; mattaḥ – from Me; eva – certainly; pṛthak-vidhāḥ – variously arranged.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"buddhiḥ\",\"translation\":\"intelligence\"},{\"word\":\"jñānam\",\"translation\":\"knowledge\"},{\"word\":\"asammohaḥ\",\"translation\":\"freedom from doubt\"},{\"word\":\"kṣamā\",\"translation\":\"forgiveness\"},{\"word\":\"satyam\",\"translation\":\"truthfulness\"},{\"word\":\"damaḥ\",\"translation\":\"control of the senses\"},{\"word\":\"śamaḥ\",\"translation\":\"control of the mind\"},{\"word\":\"sukham\",\"translation\":\"happiness\"},{\"word\":\"duḥkham\",\"translation\":\"distress\"},{\"word\":\"bhavaḥ\",\"translation\":\"birth\"},{\"word\":\"abhāvaḥ\",\"translation\":\"death\"},{\"word\":\"bhayam\",\"translation\":\"fear\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"abhayam\",\"translation\":\"fearlessness\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"also\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"and\"},{\"word\":\"ahiṁsā\",\"translation\":\"nonviolence\"},{\"word\":\"samatā\",\"translation\":\"equilibrium\"},{\"word\":\"tuṣṭiḥ\",\"translation\":\"satisfaction\"},{\"word\":\"tapaḥ\",\"translation\":\"penance\"},{\"word\":\"dānam\",\"translation\":\"charity\"},{\"word\":\"yaśaḥ\",\"translation\":\"fame\"},{\"word\":\"ayaśaḥ\",\"translation\":\"infamy\"},{\"word\":\"bhavanti\",\"translation\":\"come about\"},{\"word\":\"bhāvāḥ\",\"translation\":\"natures\"},{\"word\":\"bhūtānām\",\"translation\":\"of living entities\"},{\"word\":\"mattaḥ\",\"translation\":\"from Me\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"pṛthak-vidhāḥ\",\"translation\":\"variously arranged\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2850,\"bb\":2523,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2523/\",\"body_value\":\"Intelligence, knowledge, freedom from doubt and delusion, forgiveness, truthfulness, control of the senses, control of the mind, happiness and distress, birth, death, fear, fearlessness, nonviolence, equanimity, satisfaction, austerity, charity, fame and infamy – all these various qualities of living beings are created by Me alone.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2851,\"bb\":2524,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2524/\",\"body_value\":\"The different qualities of living entities, be they good or bad, are all created by Kṛṣṇa, and they are described here.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2852,\"bb\":2525,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2525/\",\"body_value\":\"Intelligence refers to the power to analyze things in their proper perspective, and knowledge refers to understanding what is spirit and what is matter. Ordinary knowledge obtained by a university education pertains only to matter, and it is not accepted here as knowledge. Knowledge means knowing the distinction between spirit and matter. In modern education there is no knowledge about spirit; they are simply taking care of the material elements and bodily needs. Therefore academic knowledge is not complete.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2853,\"bb\":2526,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2526/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2854,\"bb\":2527,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2527/\",\"body_value\":\"$26\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2855,\"bb\":2528,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2528/\",\"body_value\":\"$27\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2856,\"bb\":2529,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2529/\",\"body_value\":\"Ahiṁsā, nonviolence, means that one should not do anything which will put others into misery or confusion. Material activities that are promised by so many politicians, sociologists, philanthropists, etc., do not produce very good results because the politicians and philanthropists have no transcendental vision; they do not know what is actually beneficial for human society. Ahiṁsā means that people should be trained in such a way that the full utilization of the human body can be achieved. The human body is meant for spiritual realization, so any movement or any commissions which do not further that end commit violence on the human body. That which furthers the future spiritual happiness of the people in general is called nonviolence.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2857,\"bb\":2530,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2530/\",\"body_value\":\"Samatā, equanimity, refers to freedom from attachment and aversion. To be very much attached or to be very much detached is not the best. This material world should be accepted without attachment or aversion. That which is favorable for prosecuting Kṛṣṇa consciousness should be accepted; that which is unfavorable should be rejected. That is called samatā, equanimity. A person in Kṛṣṇa consciousness has nothing to reject and nothing to accept save in terms of its usefulness in the prosecution of Kṛṣṇa consciousness.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2858,\"bb\":2531,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2531/\",\"body_value\":\"$28\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2859,\"bb\":2532,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2532/\",\"body_value\":\"$29\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2860,\"bb\":2533,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2533/\",\"body_value\":\"Yaśas, fame, should be according to Lord Caitanya, who said that a man is famous when he is known as a great devotee. That is real fame. If one has become a great man in Kṛṣṇa consciousness and it is known, then he is truly famous. One who does not have such fame is infamous.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2861,\"bb\":2534,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2534/\",\"body_value\":\"All these qualities are manifest throughout the universe in human society and in the society of the demigods. There are many forms of humanity on other planets, and these qualities are there. Now, for one who wants to advance in Kṛṣṇa consciousness, Kṛṣṇa creates all these qualities, but the person develops them himself from within. One who engages in the devotional service of the Supreme Lord develops all the good qualities, as arranged by the Supreme Lord.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2862,\"bb\":2535,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/10/4-5/b2535/\",\"body_value\":\"Of whatever we find, good or bad, the origin is Kṛṣṇa. Nothing can manifest itself in this material world which is not in Kṛṣṇa. That is knowledge; although we know that things are differently situated, we should realize that everything flows from Kṛṣṇa.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 10.4-5\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 10.4-5\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\",\"$L2c\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2e:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_n